+The in-memory store removes that database access.
 
-## Shaped by
+## Known limits
 
-- [Keep sessions in the database](../adr/0001-keep-sessions-in-the-database.md)
+- Sessions disappear when the web process restarts or a release is deployed. Members must log in again afterwards.
+- Sessions are not shared between processes or web servers. In 2023, requests reaching a different server logged
+  members out, which led to the previous Postgres store. Run a single web process to keep requests on the same store;
+  multiple processes require a shared store to preserve login across them.
